\f0\b\fs70 \cf0 Apple Employee Device Usage And Security Agreement
\b0\fs24 \
\
This agreement sets forth the terms and conditions governing the use of internal devices within Apple Inc., incorporating critical information about Self Service and AppleConnect, integral tools for software installation, settings configuration, and account management.\
\
The Employee undertakes to maintain strict confidentiality regarding all aspects related to the internal devices covered by this agreement. This includes safeguarding proprietary information, security measures, and any sensitive data stored on or accessible through internal devices.\
\
Self Service is an Apple-internal tool that allows you to install relevant software, tools, and settings, including AppleConnect. Self Service collects basic information about your macOS device to recommend software or tools for you to install, or settings for you to configure.\
\
AppleConnect is an internal application used to manage and enable access to your AppleConnect account. Your AppleConnect account consists of an account name and password required to access a variety of internal company applications. Instead of having multiple account names and passwords for every internal application, the use of AppleConnect\'92s single sign-on simplifies this process.\
\
Please read the information below carefully before installing AppleConnect and related software. By using AppleConnect and related software, you agree to be bound by these terms and relevant internal policies governing the use of this software and its functionality.\
\
Use of AppleConnect to obtain access to Apple\'92s internal network requires the collection of technical and related information from your computer, including but not limited to technical information about your computer, system and application software, and peripherals. By clicking Agree, you consent to Apple\'92s collection and use of such information to facilitate access to Apple Internal Network and the provision of software updates, product support, and other services. Apple may also use information collected using AppleConnect to improve its products and services.\
\
